  "why": "One run of 64 episodes, which Netflix sells as five seasons of about 13. Netflix's seasons are real things a viewer can open, and none of them is the run: each holds a thirteenth of it. So the answer is six clusters and five containments, never a merge, and never a pick of one season as \"the\" season. The record: \"every season holds fewer than 64, rule 5's exactness refuses (a shorter first season may be one half of our run, so only exactness counts) ... any ask claim naming a season for a FINISHED run of 64 would meet guard 7's shorter direction and downgrade to PART_OF(season, run) reason count-mismatch\". The year rule that welded BAKI (anidb 12569, 26 regular episodes in three Netflix seasons of 13) is exactly what this refuses: a season whose count cannot be the run's is a part of it, whatever year it carries.",
