    "notes": "mal:5114 and the count of 64 are the record's. The Netflix title id is not (\"a Netflix title (its id is not in the record) with five seasons of about 13 each, no dates, positional numbers\"), so the title and its seasons carry the placeholder uris the record itself writes, nf:<fma> and nf:<fma>-1 to -5. 13 stands for \"about 13 each\", which is the only figure the record gives; nothing here depends on the number beyond every season holding fewer than 64. The season claims are written as PART_OF because that is how the writer takes them: the ask claim arrives as a SAME_AS naming a season and guard 7 downgrades it, part into whole by episode count. No range is claimed, because Netflix publishes no dates and retranslates its titles, so nothing per episode is known: 3.1 calls that a PART_OF and not a rangeless INCLUDES."
